Ticket #4471 originally merged 412 reports into one ticket. Analysis of tenant locales and booking forms showed that these reports covered two distinct root causes.

<Callout>
Closed. Ticket #4471 split into two dedicated tickets, both now resolved in engineering.
</Callout>

## Engineering Resolution (05 Oct 2026)

- **#1 (parser · 379 reports):** FIXED — `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`
- **#2 (hint · 33 reports):** WON'T FIX — `booking-v3 form retired`

## The Two Problems

1. **Parser reads dates month-first in day-first locales (379 reports)**
   - The shared date parser expects MM/DD/YYYY. When day-first tenants submit dates through channels without conflicting hints, dates with days ≤ 12 are inverted, or fail if days > 12.
   - Closed as completed: fixed in engineering.
   - Tracked in GitHub issue [#1](https://github.com/pyrkap/mega_dev_ch3/issues/1).

2. **Booking-v3 form displays MM/DD/YYYY hint in day-first locales (33 reports)**
   - The booking-v3 form UI shows an MM/DD/YYYY hint under the date field. Users in day-first locales follow the hint, but the form interprets inputs as day-first.
   - Closed as not planned: booking-v3 form retired.
   - Tracked in GitHub issue [#2](https://github.com/pyrkap/mega_dev_ch3/issues/2).

